    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33349" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">paedīco</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pēdīco</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Auct.
			Priap. 68</span></i>), āre, v. a.
		
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παιδικός</span>
		, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>to practise unnatural vice.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					21, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">puerum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 11, 94, 6</span></i>
			.—Of various forms of unnatural lewdness, <i><span class="en">Mart.
				11, 104, 17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. 7, 67, 1</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, of the tunic, <i><span class="en">Mart. 11,
				99, 2</span></i>.</div>
